WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.259
I have to admit that this story kind of bums
me out and you'll understand why in a little

00:00:05.259 --> 00:00:09.620
bit, it relates it relates to my youth in
some sense.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:16.930
Fox Business host Maria Bartiromo is now sinking
so low that that it's actually depressing

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:18.020
you.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.220
I am sure at this point have heard that Joe
Biden won the presidential election, that

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.100
the Electoral College confirmed it.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.550
Joe Biden has most of his cabinet selected.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:31.359
Donald Trump lost in court like 50 times or
something like that.

00:00:31.359 --> 00:00:34.650
The Supreme Court has said no thanks to his
case.

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.340
And Fox Business host Maria Bartiromo.

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:44.590
Now, really a second rate Fox host, even by
their standards, is a really aggressive Trump

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:50.360
brownnoser and claimed yesterday that an intel
source wait for it.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.890
An Intel source told her Donald Trump actually
won the election.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:01:00.210
Let's look at the clip and then I'm going
to tell you about the sort of tragic downfall

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:05.720
of Maria Bartiromo, an intel source telling
me that President Trump did, in fact, win

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.720
the election.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.170
He says that it is up to the Supreme Court
to hear suits from other cases across the

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:13.220
country to stop the clock.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:17.150
This follows the high court's refusal to hear
the lawsuit from Texas Attorney General Ken

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:18.150
Paxton.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.750
Challenging results in four swing states.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:26.890
Now, you might say, well, David, if an intel
source did tell her that she's not lying,

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:33.280
she's merely reporting it and the intel source
could simply be wrong or mistaken.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.840
But is that really the argument you want to
make?

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:37.910
That's the hill you want to die on.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:42.740
Maria Bartiromo is more than 50 years old
and she's been a journalist in some way, shape

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:45.170
or form for almost 30 years.

00:01:45.170 --> 00:01:50.710
And we're standing behind what she said is
OK and responsible to air as long as some

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:55.729
Intel person really did tell her with no vetting
or connection or actual evidence.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:58.060
She says this is what they told me.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:05.380
It's actually shocking how Maria Bartiromo
has fallen from being a great financial reporter

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.040
to being what is, in short, a conspiracy theorist.

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.040
Trump suck up.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.800
That's what she is at this point.

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.160
And the way this relates to my youth is when
I first got into trading stocks back in the

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:21.020
year 2000, when I was in high school, I started
watching CNBC because I guess that's what

00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:23.740
you do, or at least what you did at the time.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:30.890
And at the time, Maria Bartiromo really did
excellent interviews of big time Fortune 500

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:31.890
CEOs.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:33.730
She would hold them accountable for her interview.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:35.670
Preparation was second to none.

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:37.290
She was fantastic.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:41.540
And she was the first TV journalist to report
live from the floor of the New York Stock

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:42.540
Exchange.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:43.540
She won Emmys for that.

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:48.100
She was well recognized by the Italian American
community in New York City related to her

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:52.990
amazing story, working her way up from her
early days in Brooklyn as a kid, being a coat

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:54.280
checker at her dad's restaurant.

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.490
I mean, it's just an amazing story.

00:02:56.490 --> 00:03:00.060
And she was a top notch interviewer for more
than a decade.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.800
And then she joined Fox in 2013.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:05.000
Things sort of started to get a little bit
shaky.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:12.300
But then when Trump ran in 2016, she developed
like an on air relationship with Trump and

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:20.330
got to interview Donald Trump and became essentially
a dishonest PR person for Donald Trump rather

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:26.790
than a journalist, which sadly sometimes happens
to people when they go over to Fox News.

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:28.190
And it really is sad.

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:32.220
So here's my my ask of you.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:33.900
Don't let this happen to me.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:34.900
Hold me accountable.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:36.110
I don't think it would happen.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:40.599
But I'm telling you right now, if I do something
like this, you can go ahead and cancel your

00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:41.690
membership.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:47.420
It would be embarrassing and pathetic to me,
to my family, to the people that have supported

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.420
this show.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.590
But I'm sure it's lucrative for her.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:51.739
And who doesn't want to have a friend in the
White House?

00:03:51.739 --> 00:03:52.739
Right.

00:03:52.739 --> 00:03:58.980
That is that that's actually one of the things
that sometimes I think those who are only

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:06.610
very casual observers of media don't get,
which is that that the appeal of access to

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:13.500
people in power makes media people do really
crazy things sometimes.

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:20.049
And I've said before how I don't really care
about being friends with politicians.

00:04:20.049 --> 00:04:24.710
There are a number of elected officials in
the U.S. House and in other offices that that

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:26.289
I'm in touch with.

00:04:26.289 --> 00:04:30.129
And we have what I guess we would call personal
relationships.

00:04:30.129 --> 00:04:35.469
But they're not like, you know, if they do
something wrong and it's even happened, I

00:04:35.469 --> 00:04:36.610
cover it.

00:04:36.610 --> 00:04:38.219
And I'm not really impressed.

00:04:38.219 --> 00:04:42.940
I've said we shouldn't DFI these people, but
maybe when it gets to a certain level and

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:47.430
it's the president, maybe if the president
wants to be your friend, you just repeat whatever

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.270
nonsense the president wants you to say.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:51.129
I don't know.

00:04:51.129 --> 00:04:52.979
But it's really a tragedy.

00:04:52.979 --> 00:04:53.471
What's happened to Maria Bartiromo.

